      {
        "id": 224856,
        "name": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "username": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/e8c25b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-04T11:37:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Synaptic Interruption counters the electro-bombs. Choose Tachyon as the first target, and then redirect the blast back to the bomb, destroying it. If you’re making a point of feeding all of Wraith’s cards to Tachyon via her base power, you’ll draw the interruptions before the bombs hit.</p>\n<p>While normally I’m a huge fan of the Infrared Eyepiece, I think it’s nigh useless against a flipped Cosmic Omnitron and actually harmful for this particular match. The problem is those chain drone plays. The strength of the eyepiece is delay, and putting a drone on top doesn’t delay anything. So often the eyepiece has you putting a drone on the bottom and accepting a strong villain card as the top card.</p>\n<p>In this particular match the 2nd Flechettes card pretty much ends the game, and it’s buried nearly at the bottom of the deck. Every time you use the eyepiece you reduce the number of cards Omnitron has to play until it reaches it. I found this out the hard way.</p>\n<p>What you really need is a card&nbsp;that lets you&nbsp;discard from the villain’s deck, like Parse’s Extrasensory Awareness or Buffer Overflow.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:20.373Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
