      {
        "id": 224857,
        "name": "QuirkyDM",
        "username": "QuirkyDM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-04T13:20:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint for me. Negating Omnitron's damage seemed liked the order of the day, so I focused on going through Tachyon's deck to get Hypersonic Assaults. I saved Bolster Allies until the second turn so Wraith had used her power first. Wraith throat jabbed on turn 1. Tachyon used Hypersonic Assault on the next 3 turns. The only damage taken after turn 1 was when an S-84 Automaton Drone popped up.</p>\n<p>Wraith used her power exclusively to give Tachyon card draws. I did play Infrared Eyepiece, but only to use alongside Utility Belt. This meant I could use her card drawing power an extra time every turn.</p>\n<p>Legacy gave Tachyon the extra card play every turn except turn 2, where he got rid of the Self-Destruct Sequence.</p>\n<p>Absolute Zero really just kept putting out equipment and doing extra damage when he could.</p>\n<p>Bunker made sure he always had a gun out, which helps if you get Turret Mode out. Otherwise, he kept playing the cards off the top of Tachyon's deck and he did throw out an Adhesive Grenade.</p>\n<p>Tachyon blazed through her deck, using Research Grant and Pushing the Limits liberally. By the time I ran out of Hypersonic Assaults, there were 18 burst cards in her discard, so 3 Lightning Barrages and her base power finished the job easily.</p>\n<p>The only thing I would have done different was wait to play Legacy's Inspiring Presence until I was ready to use Tachyon's burst power. I also would have discarded Synaptic Interruption instead of her other bursts since I could get the other bursts into the discard pile by playing them.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:20.444Z",
