      {
        "id": 224858,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-04T16:29:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Servoret\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/91b2a8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Servoret:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mint, 8/7/19/15/10. I used TakeWalker’s hint about Fueled Freeze (which actually requires Bolster Allies and then an Onboard Module Installation play to get it out in round 1), then I focused on giving Tachyon as many draws and plays as possible to let me pull Hypersonic Assaults and finish with a Lightspeed Barrage/Blitz combo, which I did in round 5 despite a bunch of misplays that I didn’t want to take back in case I actually could pull off a Mint. I played three Hypersonic Assaults and one Throat Jab on rounds 1-4, so Omnitron never got to do damage after the first round and his EPEs never got to fire off. Thankfully his second Sedative Flechettes never came out; losing the +1 damage from Inspiring Presence might have caused me to lose the race.</p>\n<p>If you can pull Fueled Freeze right away, the Adaptive Platings aren’t an issue obviously since they both can be wiped on AZ’s first turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is the only strategy that worked for me. Preventing as much damage as possible, and giving tachyon ALL the cards with Legacy and Bunker.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Essentially i fueled her and just let absolute zero die. Used his +1 damage to help with everything.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This was a very very hard game.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:20.521Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
