      {
        "id": 224861,
        "name": "QuirkyDM",
        "username": "QuirkyDM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-05T02:13:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Gus_Smedstad\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/e8c25b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gus_Smedstad:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If I’m reading QuirkyDM’s post correctly, he didn’t do the Legacy Lead from the Front / Energy immunity thing. Instead he used Throat Jab / Hypersonic Assault x 3 / kill Omnitron in round 5. I’d have to experiment with that to see how that works out.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That’s pretty much exactly what I did. I’m trying to think if I used Heroic Interruption, so that would be an extra turn.&nbsp;Electro Pulses were out, but they were kept quiet due to Hypersonic Assault. I ignored them. The only drone&nbsp;I focused on killing was&nbsp;the one repair drone.</p>\n<p>I figure with Absolute Zero’s incap power, Legacy pulls out Inspiring Presence, Tachyon can do Burst*6&nbsp;+ 9 damage on her turn. That means 15 bursts in the discard is 99 damage. And those Hypersonic Assaults are being used in the meantime, so you wouldn’t even need that much. Omnitron was at 70 when I went to town with Tachyon, and I didn’t have boosts from Legacy or AZ.</p>\n<p>I’m also thinking that if you really focused, you could keep Omnitron on his front side by doing less than 7 damage per turn. With Throat Jab and Hypersonic Assault, you can ignore the components because all the damage comes from Omnitron.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:20.742Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
