      {
        "id": 224865,
        "name": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "username": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/e8c25b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-07T01:15:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I tried out the \"rely entirely on Throat Jab / Hypersonic Assault\" strategy, and yeah, it works.</p>\n<p>Round 1 Throat Jab.</p>\n<p>Round&nbsp;2 Inspiring Presence, Hypersonic Assault.</p>\n<p>Rounds 3-4 Hypersonic Assault.</p>\n<p>Round 5, Tachyon has drawn her entire deck, 17 Burst cards in the trash, 2x Lightspeed Barrage is enough to finish Omnitron off. No need to use Blitz.</p>\n<p>Clearly, while Tachyon does a lot of the damage, the other heroes piled on quite a bit since Omnitron is at about 30 HP at the start of round 5. An early Inspiring Presence helps, as does taking down the adaptive platings with 2x Blazing&nbsp;Speed.</p>\n<p>I didn't draw Fueled Freeze this time, which is OK, since Tachyon playing Blazing Speed adds burst cards to her trash.</p>\n<p>Rounds 1 and 2 I kept my overall damage low to avoid destroying the components and flipping Omnitron. Round 3 I found that I'd piled on enough damage that Hypersonic Assault was going to trigger it. This does delay Omnitron a little, so only one Tech Singularity comes out.</p>\n<p>Bunker used his base power rounds 1-3, whereas in my earlier game he'd draw a cannon and fired away with it. This gave Tachyon a couple of plays (once I declined to play her card because it was an early Lightspeed Barrage).</p>\n<p>Final HP was Legacy 13, Absolute Zero 2, Wraith 16, Tachyon 9, Bunker 11. Absolute Zero's health is low almost entirely because of self-harm. Tachyon took quite a few hits while drawing cards, prior to Throat Jab and in between Throat Jab and Hypersonic Assault.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:21.030Z",
